/*Q19.
Emily and Alex, two undercover spies, need to exchange sensitive information securely. They've devised a method to encode their messages into binary strings and share them through a secure channel. To decode the messages, they perform XOR (exclusive OR) operations on the binary strings.

Write a Java program to assist Emily and Alex in decoding their messages by performing XOR operations on binary strings.

Input Format:
  - The first two lines of the input are binary codes representing the encoded messages.

Output Format:
  - The output is an integer representing the result after performing the XOR operation.

Note: A partial code is provided in the editor.*/
//////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////
/*Logic: Same as Q15.*/

import java.util.Scanner;

public class Main {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        Scanner sc = new Scanner(System.in);
        long a = Long.parseLong(sc.next().trim(), 2);
        long b = Long.parseLong(sc.next().trim(), 2);
        System.out.println(a ^ b);
        sc.close();
    }
}
